# Licences allowed for the Python distributions in the gippa-step images (M11-15 item 8a).
# scripts/release/check_image_licences.py reads it; GIPPA stays MIT (Q-K34): permissive only.
# One entry per line: an SPDX identifier (or "<id> WITH <exception>"), a value of the core
# metadata License field, or a "License ::" trove classifier. Matching ignores case.
MIT
MIT-CMU
BSD-2-Clause
BSD-3-Clause
0BSD
Apache-2.0
Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
ISC
Zlib
CC0-1.0
PSF-2.0
Python-2.0
# certifi: file-level copyleft, shipped unmodified (lead decision, M11-15g).
MPL-2.0
# Biopython License Agreement: permissive (biopython is dual-licensed with BSD-3-Clause).
LicenseRef-Biopython-License-Agreement
# License field values without a version: every BSD variant is permissive.
BSD
Public-Domain
License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License
License :: OSI Approved :: BSD License
License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License
License :: OSI Approved :: Python Software Foundation License
License :: OSI Approved :: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL 2.0)
License :: Public Domain
